<!--
Copy to .cursor/rules/{rule-name}.mdc in your project.

The extension MUST be .mdc: Cursor ignores plain .md files in .cursor/rules
because they carry no frontmatter.

Frontmatter selects when the rule loads:
  alwaysApply: true             -> every conversation; globs and description ignored
  globs: src/**/*.ts            -> attached when a matching file is in context
  description: <text>           -> Agent pulls it in when the description is relevant
  neither globs nor description -> only when @-mentioned in chat

Project-wide context (stack, commands, architecture) belongs in AGENTS.md,
which Cursor reads from the project root and from subdirectories. Keep this
file for rules that need scoping, and keep it under 500 lines.
-->

